# Daily logs are append-only: when two devices both add entries to the same
# day, the correct merge is to keep both sides' lines. That is precisely what
# git's built-in `union` low-level merge driver does, so same-day edits from
# two machines merge silently instead of producing conflict markers.
#
# This is the single most important line in a synced Memoria store.
memories/daily/*.md merge=union

# Everything else takes the normal three-way merge: core memories are edited,
# not appended, so a genuine conflict there deserves a human.
*.md text eol=lf
